TITLE='Authentic title "The SpaceX IPO Is About To Flip Your 401k - Most People Are Not Ready" is an urgent news-hook frame. The script\'s actual argument is that SpaceX is not in most 401(k)s (S&P 500 rules exclude it until at least 2027) and that the real change is the August 2025 private-assets executive order; the title\'s "flip your 401k" is delivered only indirectly.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background: the recurring cartoon man laughing with excitement; "ARE YOU READY?!" in heavy black capitals; a chart in which a flat "401K" line turns into a soaring green "SPACEX" line, with an arrow at the turn. At 320x180 the words and chart read clearly. The image implies SpaceX will boost 401(k)s, which contradicts the script\'s cautionary thesis.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator 52-minute explainer with two composites (Logan buys IPO shares; Dana owns a target-date fund): the IPO facts, retail allocation, S&P 500 eligibility rules and the 4 June 2026 rejection, the Nasdaq-100 and MSCI exceptions, index-inclusion forced buying (Tesla), lockup risk, the August 2025 executive order, a steelman, three problems (fees, illiquidity, late-stage access), valuation (94x revenue; Morningstar $780B), shrinking public markets, the players and skeptics, side-door funds (DXYZ, ARK, Baron), IPO first-day history, the Logan/Dana payoff, four actions and a community promotion. Core facts verify; the 70,000% and 62,000% figures, the SPACE ticker and the Tesla run-up are wrong.'
